  "reason": "Evidence: Multi-profile with avgpool aggregation is clearly the strongest setting (config_008 rna_only=0.5305, config_002 multimodal=0.5121), and avgpool outperforms transformer aggregation (0.5121 vs 0.4710). Notably, the RNA-only model (config_008) slightly outperforms the multimodal counterpart (config_002) by ~1.8%, suggesting the image modality with concat fusion may not be contributing effectively. Question: Is the suboptimal fusion strategy (concat) the reason the image modality underperforms? Config_048 isolates a single variable—changing fusion from concat to weighted—while holding model_setting, profile_setting, rna_encoder, image_encoder, and aggregation identical to config_002. This gives a clean A/B comparison on fusion and a three-way benchmark against config_008 (RNA-only). Why best next step: It is the most targeted experiment to determine whether the image channel can be made useful with scgpt+resnet50, which directly informs whether to invest remaining budget in image-encoder or fusion variations versus committing to RNA-only or alternative RNA encoders. A single-variable change maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
